node_modules/
dist/
server/data/
*.log
.worktrees/
.scratch/

# Scratch files from exploratory runs -- probes, repros, one-off scripts. They belong in a
# temp dir, but an agent or a hurried session drops one in the root now and then, and `git add
# -A` then sweeps it into a commit. Ignored so that cannot happen silently.
__probe*
probe*.ts
_*probe*
repro.ts
**/__tmp_*
# Agents keep inventing new spellings for the same thing (zzprobe-*, *_probe_tmp, scratch-*),
# so match the WORD anywhere rather than a fixed prefix. A real test file never has "probe",
# "scratch" or "tmp" in its name -- it is named after what it tests.
*probe*
*scratch*
*_tmp*
*tmp_*
